      ],
      "id": "fig-f19-6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Our analysis only considers the impact of `avexpr` on economic performance. However, numerous other factors influencing income per capita are not included in the model. Omitting these variables that affect `logpgp95` can lead to omitted variable bias. @Acemoglu2001 consider the following factors:\n",
        "\n",
        "* Cultural, historical, and other contextual factors, which are accounted for through the inclusion of continent dummy variables.\n",
        "* Climate proxied by latitude (`lat_abst`).\n",
        "\n",
        "We estimate some of the extended models considered by @Acemoglu2001 using data in the `maketable2.dta` file. The results are presented in @tbl-t19-6. The coefficient estimate for the protection against expropriation index is statistically significant at the 1% level across all three models. The relationship remains robust to the inclusion of additional controls, such as geography and continent dummies."
      ],
      "id": "0fd25679"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df2 = pd.read_stata('data/maketable2.dta')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Estimate an OLS regression for each set of variables using smf.ols\n",
        "reg1 = smf.ols(formula='logpgp95 ~ avexpr', data=df2).fit(vcov=\"HC1\")\n",
        "reg2 = smf.ols(formula='logpgp95 ~ avexpr + lat_abst', data=df2).fit(vcov=\"HC1\")\n",
        "reg3 = smf.ols(formula='logpgp95 ~ avexpr + lat_abst + asia + africa + other', data=df2).fit(vcov=\"HC1\")"
      ],
      "id": "cef96743",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::{layout-ncol=1}"
      ],
      "id": "ccb27be5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| tbl-cap: The OLS estimation results\n",
        "#| label: tbl-t19-6\n",
        "info_dict={'R-squared' : lambda x: f\"{x.rsquared:.2f}\",\n",
        "           'No. observations' : lambda x: f\"{int(x.nobs):d}\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "results_table = summary_col(results=[reg1,reg2,reg3],\n",
        "                            float_format='%0.2f',\n",
        "                            stars = True,\n",
        "                            model_names=['Model 1',\n",
        "                                         'Model 3',\n",
        "                                         'Model 4'],\n",
        "                            info_dict=info_dict,\n",
        "                            regressor_order=['const',\n",
        "                                             'avexpr',\n",
        "                                             'lat_abst',\n",
        "                                             'asia',\n",
        "                                             'africa'])\n",
        "results_table"
      ],
      "id": "tbl-t19-6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "@Acemoglu2001 highlight several critical reasons to exercise caution when interpreting the estimation results given in @tbl-t19-6 as causal:\n",
        "\n",
        "* Omitted variable bias: There are unobserved determinants of income differences that are naturally correlated with institutions.\n",
        "* Simultaneous causality bias: Wealthier nations are more likely to invest in and develop better institutional frameworks.\n",
        "* Error-in-variables bias: The construction of the institutional index may be subject to biases. For instance, analysts might be predisposed to view countries with higher incomes as having superior institutions.\n",
        "\n",
        "We can solve all of these problems by using a valid instrument for institutions (`avexpr`). The instrument must be:\n",
        "\n",
        "* correlated with `avexpr` (instrument relevance),\n",
        "* not correlated with the error term $u$ (instrument exogeneity). \n",
        "\n",
        "The primary contribution of @Acemoglu2001 lies in their use of \"settler mortality rates\" (`logem4`) as an instrument for institutional differences. They propose that settler mortality influenced settlement patterns, which in turn shaped early institutions. These early institutions persisted over time, ultimately forming the foundation of current institutional frameworks. This hypothesis is illustrated in @fig-f19-4."
      ],
      "id": "e6bb263f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| fig-cap: From settler mortality to current institutions\n",
        "#| label: fig-f19-4\n",
        "# Create a directed graph\n",
        "G = nx.DiGraph()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Add nodes and edges\n",
        "G.add_edge(\"Settler Mortality\", \"Settlements\")\n",
        "G.add_edge(\"Settlements\", \"Early Institutions\")\n",
        "G.add_edge(\"Early Institutions\", \"Current Institutions\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Define positions for the nodes\n",
        "pos = {\n",
        "    \"Settler Mortality\": (0, 0),\n",
        "    \"Settlements\": (0.5, 0),\n",
        "    \"Early Institutions\": (1, 0),\n",
        "    \"Current Institutions\": (1.5, 0)\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "# Draw the graph\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(5.5, 1.5))\n",
        "nx.draw(G, pos, with_labels=True, node_size=4500, node_color=\"skyblue\", font_size=8, arrowsize=10)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-f19-4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "To check instrument relevance, we generate a scatterplot of `avexpr` against `logem4` (log settler mortality rate). @fig-f19-7 reveals a negative correlation between protection against expropriation and settler mortality rates, consistent with the authors' hypothesis. This negative relationship indicates that higher settler mortality rates are associated with lower levels of protection against expropriation during 1985–95. The first stage F-statistic is 31.5, which is greater than 10, indicating that the instrument is relevant."
      ],
      "id": "487fb1ad"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| fig-cap: First-stage relationship between settler mortality and expropriation risk\n",
        "#| label: fig-f19-7\n",
        "# Dropping NA's is required to use numpy's polyfit\n",
        "df1_subset2 = df1.dropna(subset=['logem4', 'avexpr'])\n",
        "\n",
        "X = df1_subset2['logem4']\n",
        "y = df1_subset2['avexpr']\n",
        "labels = df1_subset2['shortnam']\n",
        "\n",
        "# Replace markers with country labels\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5, 4))\n",
        "ax.scatter(X, y, marker='')\n",
        "\n",
        "for i, label in enumerate(labels):\n",
        "    ax.annotate(label, (X.iloc[i], y.iloc[i]), fontsize=8)\n",
        "\n",
        "# The first stage regression\n",
        "m1 = smf.ols(formula='avexpr ~ logem4', data=df1_subset2).fit(vcov=\"HC1\")\n",
        "predictions = m1.predict(df1_subset2['logem4'])\n",
        "ax.plot(df1_subset2['logem4'], predictions, color='steelblue', linewidth=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "ax.set_xlim([1.8,8.4])\n",
        "ax.set_ylim([3.3,10.4])\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel('Log of settler mortality')\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel('Average expropriation risk 1985-95')\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-f19-7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# The first stage F-statistic\n",
        "m1.f_test(\"logem4 = 0\")"
      ],
      "id": "643273a2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The instrument exogeneity condition may not be satisfied if settler mortality rates in the 17th to 19th centuries have a direct effect on current GDP (in addition to their indirect effect through institutions). For example, settler mortality rates may be related to the current disease environment in a country, which could affect current economic performance. @Acemoglu2001 argue this is unlikely because:\n",
        "\n",
        "* The majority of settler deaths were due to malaria and yellow fever and these diseases had a limited effect on local people.\n",
        "* The disease burden on local people in Africa or India, for example, did not appear to be higher than average, supported by relatively high population densities in these areas before colonization.\n",
        "  \n",
        "Hence, the settler mortality rate variable seem to be a valid instrument and we can proceed with the TSLS estimation. The estimation results are presented in @tbl-t19-7. The estimated coefficient on the protection against expropriation index is 0.94, with a standard error of 0.18. The coefficient is statistically significant at the 5% level. Compared to the OLS estimate (0.53), the TSLS estimate is larger, suggesting that the OLS estimate is biased downwards. "
      ],
      "id": "f1e8b49f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "message": false
      },
      "source": [
        "#| warning: false\n",
        "# Using only mortality rate as the instrument\n",
        "# Import and select the data\n",
        "df4 = pd.read_stata('data/maketable4.dta')\n",
        "df4 = df4[df4['baseco'] == 1]\n",
        "\n",
        "model = IV2SLS.from_formula(\n",
        "    formula=\"logpgp95 ~ 1 + [avexpr ~ logem4]\",\n",
        "    data=df4\n",
        ").fit(cov_type='robust')"
      ],
      "id": "43dac164",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::{layout-ncol=1}"
      ],
      "id": "91a91fc9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| tbl-cap: The TSLS estimation results\n",
        "#| label: tbl-t19-7\n",
        "# Create Stargazer table\n",
        "stargazer = Stargazer([model])\n",
        "stargazer.significant_digits(3)\n",
        "stargazer.show_degrees_of_freedom(False)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Render Stargazer object\n",
        "stargazer"
      ],
      "id": "tbl-t19-7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
